«
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  @  UShapeQ
  @  Quantile: the X below which the probability is p.
  @  Author & design          : Jean Wilson
  @  Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @  Arguments may be given loose or bundled in a list of 3; that list is
  @  what LastArguments reports, and its length is checked before use.
  @  The arc sine law inverts in closed form: its distribution function
  @  (2/π)·asin(√((X−Xmin)/(Xmax−Xmin))) gives X = Xmin + (Xmax−Xmin)·sin²(π·p/2).
  @  The angle is in radians whatever the angle mode, and p is kept in [0, 1].
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  IF DUP TypeName "list" == THEN IF DUP Size 3 ≠ THEN "UShapeQ: needs 3 arguments" DoError END Explode Drop END
  → Xminv Xmaxv pv « Xminv 0 + Xmaxv 0 + pv 0 + → Xmin Xmax p « 'IFTE(p≤0;Xmin;IFTE(p≥1;Xmax;Xmin+(Xmax-Xmin)*SIN(Ⓒπ*p/2*1_r)^2))' →Num Xminv Xmaxv pv 3 →List Drop » »
»
